6cl|a|Of or pertaining to an axis; of the nature of, or resembling, an axis; around an axis. ; Belonging to the axis of the body; as, the axial skeleton; or to the axis of any appendage or organ; as, the axial bones.	j:tfu,116,4;tep,102,8;m5e,79,3;v9y,77,3~tep,102,8;tfu,116,4;m5e,79,3;v9y,77,3
6cx|a|A self-evident and necessary truth, or a proposition whose truth is so evident as first sight that no reasoning or demonstration can make it plainer; a proposition which it is necessary to take for granted; as, "The whole is greater than a part;" "A thing can not, at the same time, be and not be." ; An established principle in some art or science, which, though not a necessary truth, is universally received; as, the axioms of political economy.	j:2784,42,4~2784,42,4
